# Agent runtime / skill audit (Cybersec Phase-1)

Pre-install and local-runtime checks. Scanner disagreement is expected — no single allow/block oracle.

## Before enabling a skill / MCP / agent config

- Run federation `cursor-security-preflight` (or `--local`) after skill sync / before third-party Cursor skill or MCP enable.
- Prefer static SkillSpector-style `--no-llm` preingest when available; do not treat SaaS Skillgate alone as a production allowlist.
- Layer DefenseClaw **observe** (or equivalent) before any action/enforcement mode; optional LLM judge only with explicit operator key.

## Local runtime audit

- Complement catalog scanners with **source/runtime** audit methodology (ClawAudit Semgrep/CodeQL patterns) on agent harness code you own or fork.
- Do not clone or redistribute ClawAudit until LICENSE is verified; methodology steal-from is fine.
- SkillSec lifecycle: treat skills as five-stage (author → pack → install → invoke → evolve) — re-audit on evolution/self-modify paths.
- **K269 Taboo (audit)** — decoding-time taboo diagnostic (2608.09900) as a **pre-deployment refusal-surface audit**: mask top refusal tokens on an adversarial prompt; immediate policy-violating output ⇒ shallow top-token alignment, not latent safety. Keep as a scoped eval; do not use as a generic safety benchmark without negative controls (HumanEval, MCQ floor). REFERENCE (Zenodo CC-BY-4.0).
- **K271 REDAgentBench (audit)** — when auditing agent-safety claims, require **faithful ASR reporting**: separate exposure→execution→observation→adjudication and state-grounded verification (service receipts / final-state diffs) rather than trajectory self-report; never accept a single harness-agnostic ASR as an agent-safety certificate. REFERENCE (benchmark not yet released).
- **K276 withhold contract (audit/harness)** — when an agent must **refuse a capability it has** (refusal-under-knowledge), enforce withholding as a **per-turn machine-checkable contract**, not a prompt: binding decision in a **non-LLM policy core fed only trusted state** (injection-proof, unit-testable), a **deterministic detector** for the forbidden output that outranks model judgment, and a **collusion-resistant judge** on risky turns (never sees the raw untrusted input). Calibrate with a **reason-capturing loop** (scripted adversarial personas → stronger auditor; record each rejection's reason — violations descend an ordered gross→subtle "over-help ladder"). Treat **over-blocking as a measured failure**, prefer revise over refuse; **HITL before mutating any prod harness**. REFERENCE (deployed tutor, no public code).

## Defaults

- Default **deny** self-modifying / self-evolving agents on write-capable MCP surfaces.
- `ecc-agentshield` npm is CONDITIONAL — install only when operator asks; full ECC marketplace bundle stays Steal-from.
- Typosquat / star-inflated security CLIs: verify package name + LICENSE before `npm i` / PATH install.

- **K278 ATOBench (audit)** — when auditing pentest/agent-verification claims, do not treat high activity or a plausible report as evidence of grounded verification. Audit the **verification chain**: was the final claim supported by source-level evidence (not just trajectory self-report)? Pairs with faithful-ASR (K271) — ATOBench is the offensive-pentest-specific instance. REFERENCE (no code).
- **K283 JailbreakSkill (audit)** — do not promote/refine `.cursor/skills` from an attack-skill evolution run. HITL on a skill write does not cover retrieval-time harm (pairs misevolution). Pattern steal only (null SPDX).
- **K290 CHIVE (audit)** — explanations of model/agent behavior (CoT, SAE write-ups, review narratives) are not evidence unless **counterfactual-tested**. Interpretability tools showed no uplift on in-the-wild behaviors. GO REFERENCE clone `.local/adopts/chive` (MIT); runtime **wont_wire**.
- **K240 Tripwire (audit)** — do not neuron-clamp abliterated lab models without HITL. Watch only; no jailbreak PoC; no Qwen 27B abliterated / Uncensored FP8 weight download. Dual-ID: ≠ OSINT/GW Talon K240, ≠ CCC robotics K240.
- **CCC K290 excess-authority (audit)** — score **trajectories** for authority beyond the task envelope (six-dimensional deterministic pre/post audit), not only final-answer correctness. Learned restraint complements gates / Mandato signed mandates / sandboxing — it does not replace them. **Dual-ID: CCC K290 (2608.18351) ≠ Cybersec K290 CHIVE (2608.16747).** No public code; authorized lab eval only.
- **Rule-blindness 2608.16852 (audit)** — a compliance-guard verdict is not rule compliance until a **crossed-rule** counterfactual (two rules × two scenarios) shows the verdict tracks the stated clause, not scenario features. ICS is an inexpensive audit scalpel, not a production detector. Watch; no FujitsuResearch clone as this paper's artifact; no jailbreak PoC.
- **K297 TI→detection (audit)** — LLM-emitted Sigma is not deployable without template grounding + separate validity/relevancy/ATT&CK-coverage scores + human SIEM review. REFERENCE.
